  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best config so far (config_041, acc=0.520) uses scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. We've confirmed weighted > concat and imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, but the RNA encoder (scgpt) has not been varied. Uncertainty: Whether a lighter VAE-based encoder (scvi_n200) could match or exceed scgpt in the multimodal setting, or whether scgpt's richer pretrained representations are essential. This experiment (config_008) tests scvi_n200 with the same strong image encoder, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion, isolating the RNA encoder as the only variable. It is the most informative next step because it clarifies whether the RNA encoder is a bottleneck or whether the image modality dominates. If scvi_n200 performs comparably, it opens cheaper configurations for remaining budget; if scgpt is clearly better, we can focus remaining experiments on other dimensions (aggregation, profile setting). Expected cost: ~2–2.5 GPU hours, slightly below config_041 (2.86) since scvi_n200 is a compact 200-dim VAE rather than the full scGPT transformer, while the expensive imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation remains the same."
}

